              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The thin, lightweight shirts in Columbia's **PFG (Performance Fishing Gear)** line typically go by a few different names depending on whether you are looking for a button-down shirt or an athletic sun shirt:\n\n### 1. The Button-Down: **Columbia Tamiami (or Tamiami II)**\nIf you are thinking of the classic button-down fishing shirt with front pockets and a vented back, but in an ultra-thin, silky, and featherlight fabric, you are thinking of the **Tamiami**. \n* **Material:** 100% lightweight polyester ripstop.\n* **Features:** It is by far Columbia's lightest and thinnest button-down shirt. It has a very airy, almost weightless feel, dries incredibly fast, and features UPF 40 sun protection.\n\n### 2. The T-Shirt / Hoodie style: **Columbia Terminal Tackle**\nIf the shirt you have in mind is a long-sleeve athletic shirt (with or without a hood) rather than a button-down, it is called the **Terminal Tackle**. \n* **Material:** Thin, smooth polyester knit (feels like a silky, lightweight gym shirt).\n* **Features:** It is designed to be worn directly against the skin as a sun guard (UPF 50) and is highly breathable and moisture-wicking.\n\n---\n\n### How they compare to other Columbia PFG shirts:\nTo help you make sure you get the right one, here is how the thin models compare to Columbia's other famous PFG shirts:\n* **The Bahama (Bahama II):** This is a nylon button-down. While it is quick-drying and lighter than cotton, the nylon fabric is noticeably stiffer, crisper, and thicker than the polyester *Tamiami*.\n* **The Bonehead:** This is a cotton button-down. It is the heaviest and thickest shirt in the PFG lineup. While comfortable, it gets heavy when wet and does not wick moisture well.\n* **The Slack Tide:** A thin, soft, polyester-blend camp shirt with a modern, laid-back collar. It is lightweight and thin like the Tamiami, but styled more like a casual summer shirt rather than a utility fishing shirt.",
